  "limits": [
    "A paper is reached through the identifier the model repository records, by PubMed id or by DOI. An entry naming no paper cannot be reached, and several entries name the same paper, so the entry count is a floor and not a paper count.",
    "'A results table' is read off propose_claims: a table whose candidates state a metric is naming quantities a reproduction targets. That is a signal, not a proof, so the per-table counts are kept.",
    "Each entry's model format and curation status travel beside its paper, because a paper stating reproducible results is only half of what a certificate needs: an entry shipping an R script or a non-curated hybrid cannot be run whatever its paper says."
  ],
